7592186045417] [17592186304962 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ ⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312052 #edb/ref 1080 "(-9,9,7)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312052 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312052 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a523b91-b0c8-5d77-ac05-a918d500094c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312080 #edb/ref 1080 "(-20,31,13)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312080 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312080 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0eb8f532-8109-56ef-8ea6-7d7e8fda174e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312369 #edb/ref 1080 "(-20,13,31)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312369 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312369 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313028 #edb/ref 1080 "No intersection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313028 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313028 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "82d8d2f3-12d7-5f69-9c67-b4d2db7dc5da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313102 #edb/ref 1080 "(5,-1,3)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313102 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 175921