db/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342124 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7b7455d-19c2-5862-8ffa-6bf81d08e53f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342124 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342125 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342125 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342125 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342125 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342125 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a27e98ee-3a96-559d-b75b-2bf4d0ce11d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342125 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342127 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342127 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342127 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342127 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a17e320-306c-50fa-b84b-f8cbe958e629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342127 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342128 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74003" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342128 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342128 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342128 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d4d8f0f-1eab-5bd0-8f71-a26637e6257d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342128 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399608 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399608 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108309" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399608 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399608 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399608 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "310a805e-d3a4-5eae-9540-0ee13a3dc212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399608 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399609 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218639